WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.037 --> 00:00:02.080
- You just had a big birthday.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.284
- I did. 30. 30 y'all.

00:00:04.284 --> 00:00:06.157
(audience cheering)

00:00:06.157 --> 00:00:08.970
- What did you do? How did you celebrate?

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.890
- I was actually in Rome at a friends-

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:13.640
- As you are on your birthday. Yes.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.740
- I was actually at a friends wedding,

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.600
which was crazy. Mikey Hess.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.300
Yeah, Paul McCartney was there.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.940
Katy Perry was there.
- Oh, wow.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:22.950
Ellie Goulding.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.160
- Nobody knows them, yeah.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.530
- No it was insane, insane.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:27.750
The craziest wedding I've ever seen.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.810
- Wow. So you got to celebrate there

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.520
and then after you did something, right?

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:32.690
- Absolutely. I'm still celebrating.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:34.121
I'm celebrating right now!

00:00:34.121 --> 00:00:35.845
(audience applauding)

00:00:35.845 --> 00:00:38.290
- [Kelly] I saw a video of
you, actually in Europe,

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:39.540
performing on a balcony

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.600
and I was curious what you were doing.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.326
- Oh. Prague I think it was.

00:00:44.326 --> 00:00:45.159
- I don't know.

00:00:45.159 --> 00:00:46.910
You were on a balcony with a megaphone.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:48.176
- Yes, so what happened was-

00:00:48.176 --> 00:00:49.652
- I was like, "Get to 'em!"

00:00:49.652 --> 00:00:51.180
He was like, "You're
gonna hear this music."

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.013
What happened?

00:00:52.013 --> 00:00:55.670
- So the venue wasn't safe
so I didn't want to continue

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:58.320
with the show so we
had to cancel the show.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.980
But there was just so many people outside

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.830
and I felt crazy, you know?

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:04.033
It was, obviously, I was on tour.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:06.830
- And artists feel horrible
when you have to cancel.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.350
People don't get that, you feel horrible.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:09.183
- [Jason] Feel terrible.

00:01:09.183 --> 00:01:10.677
I mean it's people's birthday gifts.

00:01:10.677 --> 00:01:12.336
They spent their last dollars.

00:01:12.336 --> 00:01:13.860
- They took their night off from work.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.860
- 100%. So we got a makeshift performance.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.150
We brought out two little speakers.

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:24.280
I got on a little mic
and I sang the songs.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.720
I even had my dancers
come out on the balcony.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.170
They would come in and make an appearance

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:32.332
and they'd do a little
dance and then go backstage.

00:01:32.332 --> 00:01:33.410
- I think that that's awesome.

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:35.360
You constantly tour the world, though.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:36.680
Is there a favorite place for you?

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:37.840
I have a couple that I love.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.279
- Woo. Sydney, Australia is probably-

00:01:40.279 --> 00:01:41.959
- Australia is one of my favorites.

00:01:41.959 --> 00:01:43.540
- Yeah, yeah me too.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:44.400
- It's so good.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.233
- It is so good.

00:01:45.233 --> 00:01:46.066
- They're so chill.

00:01:46.066 --> 00:01:47.290
They're so ready for a hang.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:48.890
- They chill.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:51.990
It's kinda like they're living to live

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:53.849
and not living to work, necessarily.

00:01:53.849 --> 00:01:54.690
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:56.045
- Sometimes they take
offense when I say that

00:01:56.045 --> 00:01:57.610
cause like, "What you
think, we ain't got no job?"

00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:58.950
Nah, nah, nah, nah.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.757
- No it's 'cause we work 24-7 all the time

00:02:00.757 --> 00:02:02.800
and we don't really
experience life sometimes.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.200
- For sure. And they
ain't got not road rage.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.487
You can cut somebody
off and they'd be like,

00:02:05.487 --> 00:02:07.518
"Have it your way, Bro, it's all good."

00:02:07.518 --> 00:02:08.920
(audience laughing)

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:11.650
In America, they ready
to get out of their cars.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.840
It's like, "Bro, I put my signal on.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.217
G, like chill."

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:17.987
- You're hilarious.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.530
- My mom doesn't think I'm hilarious.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.840
She's like, "No, Joey's the funny one."

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:23.940
I'm like, Ma.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:25.655
- I got game too!

00:02:25.655 --> 00:02:26.745
You're hilarious.

00:02:26.745 --> 00:02:28.580
No, I love your timing.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.220
You had a life changing
realization last year.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:32.070
Tell us about it.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:32.903
- [Jason] Oh yes.

00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:35.227
So I kind of work all the time.

00:02:35.227 --> 00:02:37.067
I'm a 24-7 worker.
- Me too.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.210
I mean I get up in the morning,
I'm thinking about work.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.620
You know how that is.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.470
So, I was like,

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:42.790
if I'm going to be working this hard

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:44.500
I gotta live life.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.800
You can not do one without the other.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.610
So I made it a point to
actually go out and do things.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:51.990
Cause you know how you
go to certain countries

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:52.823
and you don't see the country.

00:02:52.823 --> 00:02:53.670
- You don't see it
- Yeah.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.920
- The venue was nice.
The airport was lovely.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.110
- Exactly. But I'm not doing that no more.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.590
So I'm gonna go out there
and I'm gonna live life

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.310
and I'm gonna do things
- That's good.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:04.270
for the rest of my life
- That's so important.

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:05.763
and it's been unbelievable.

00:03:06.922 --> 00:03:08.030
- That's so important.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.340
I have to say this because
when I saw you in your room,

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:11.910
I didn't check out your whole side.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.440
Look at your hair right now.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.721
- Yeah. I'm going to do the
rest of the interview like this.

00:03:15.721 --> 00:03:16.770
Don't even trip.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:17.889
- Great profile.

00:03:17.889 --> 00:03:20.930
Has there ever been anything
that you are too afraid to do?

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:24.210
'Cause I always see you
doing lots of crazy stuff.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.043
- You know.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:28.388
Black people, we don't really
like jumping out of planes.

00:03:28.388 --> 00:03:30.770
- I'm white and I ain't
jumping out of a plane.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:31.603
- Okay, so we on the same page.

00:03:31.603 --> 00:03:32.690
- Why a perfectly good airplane.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.090
Why the hell am I jumping out of it?

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:35.043
- Why? Why?

00:03:35.043 --> 00:03:36.780
I just don't like the falling motion.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:37.960
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.740
So I did do something cool.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.246
I hung off a building,
- Nope.

00:03:41.246 --> 00:03:42.330
I aint' drop though.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:45.230
I was hanging off the side.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.949
- [Kelly] Oh hell now!

00:03:46.949 --> 00:03:48.440
- [Jason] Look at the fear.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:49.483
I'm so scared!

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:51.680
He was like, "Give me a high five."

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:52.513
I'm like, ugh.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.193
- I have to ask you. Why?

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:57.903
- It's that thing.

00:03:57.903 --> 00:04:00.700
It's like just doing
things because, you know?

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:01.860
It's just exhilarating.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.710
- That's when I just eat some cake.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:08.523
Or have a really good cup of coffee.

00:04:08.523 --> 00:04:10.493
- That's also amazing.
- [Kelly] It is.

00:04:10.493 --> 00:04:12.070
You can do it all though!

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:14.280
You can have the cake
on top of a building.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.843
- Hell no. Nope. I'm not your girl..

